speechtext:
For a copy of all letters, telegrams, and other documents, memorandums, protests, recommendations, and reports of officials of the Post Office Department, and of the Civil Service Commission, in the possession of the Civil Commission, relating to:
1.	The appointments, qualifications, rejections, of any person or persons in charge of the post office at Hawkesbury, Ontario, from the year 1922 to date;
2.	The appointment or rejection of one -MacA1 lister as postmaster at Hawkesbury;
3.	The appointment, temporary or otherwise, of a successor to the said MacAllister.
